Northwest Territories Act the commissioner should be an officer of the department of northern affairs and thus in a position to co-ordinate the policies of the territorial administration in relation to the people of the territory generally with the special federal responsibilities and policies concerning the Eskimo people who will constitute the majority of the population of the new territory, at least in its early years.
